00:04:03,940 --> 00:04:08,140
So the genetic testing that the oncology department

00:04:08,140 --> 00:04:11,300
is going to do is going to be for some very specific genes

00:04:11,300 --> 00:04:14,780
that can have tendencies to run into family,

00:04:14,780 --> 00:04:17,780
that could be a cause of cancer.

00:04:17,780 --> 00:04:22,420
Now, they can do some genes that we can't do.

00:04:22,420 --> 00:04:25,460
Now, there are genes that they will typically run

00:04:25,460 --> 00:04:28,100
when they do that study and what are the bronchagines.

00:04:28,100 --> 00:04:30,260
So this person says I was always under the impression

00:04:30,260 --> 00:04:32,900
that even if they found the bronchagines

00:04:32,900 --> 00:04:34,460
or other mutations,

00:04:34,460 --> 00:04:37,500
that should not really change my treatment decisions.

00:04:37,500 --> 00:04:39,540
Or would it be helpful to know

00:04:39,540 --> 00:04:41,900
if there are any other cancer related genes lurking

00:04:41,900 --> 00:04:43,540
in my DNA?

00:04:43,540 --> 00:04:46,660
My answer to this is if they're willing to run this test

00:04:46,660 --> 00:04:49,620
and your insurance is going to cover it by all means,

00:04:49,620 --> 00:04:50,900
I'd say go for it.

00:04:50,900 --> 00:04:53,180
Yes, run the gene, run the test.

00:04:53,180 --> 00:04:56,060
Now, when we also look in our genetic profile,

00:04:56,060 --> 00:04:58,180
we look at your bronchagines, too.

00:04:58,180 --> 00:05:03,180
Now, there are, all your genes have family of genes.

00:05:03,940 --> 00:05:06,340
So your bronchagines are a family of genes.

00:05:06,340 --> 00:05:10,260
There's actually about around 100 different bronchagines.

00:05:11,220 --> 00:05:14,740
Now, there's really only, when they do a test for you,

00:05:14,740 --> 00:05:16,140
when the oncologist does a test,

00:05:16,140 --> 00:05:18,540
they're really looking at about three or four of the bronchagines

00:05:18,540 --> 00:05:23,260
because those have been tied to the most significant ones

00:05:23,260 --> 00:05:29,940
that can lead to an inability to fight cancer.

00:05:29,940 --> 00:05:32,940
So, I just said, your bronchagines are tumor suppressor genes.

00:05:34,300 --> 00:05:37,500
There are numerous different families

00:05:37,660 --> 00:05:40,740
of tumor suppressor genes like the bronchagines

00:05:40,740 --> 00:05:44,900
that if you have mutations, slash defects of those genes,

00:05:44,900 --> 00:05:47,620
those genes won't work as well.

00:05:47,620 --> 00:05:48,620
Why is that important?

00:05:48,620 --> 00:05:51,540
Because tumor suppressor genes turn on

00:05:51,540 --> 00:05:55,620
when a cell goes into rapid replication

00:05:55,620 --> 00:05:59,180
and it turns on and it stimulates

00:05:59,180 --> 00:06:01,340
apoptosis of the cell.

00:06:01,340 --> 00:06:04,500
So it can turn on and stimulate cell death

00:06:04,500 --> 00:06:08,140
so that that's one way that God put in us

00:06:08,140 --> 00:06:10,060
to be able to fight against cancer

00:06:10,060 --> 00:06:11,580
because remember, we've said,

00:06:11,580 --> 00:06:13,140
what are the struggles with cancer?

00:06:13,140 --> 00:06:15,580
Is that cancer is your own cells?

00:06:15,580 --> 00:06:17,540
Something gets inside the cell,

00:06:17,540 --> 00:06:22,180
damages the DNA, causes the DNA to go into rapid replication.

00:06:22,180 --> 00:06:23,020
What could it be?

00:06:23,020 --> 00:06:23,900
Could it be a toxin?

00:06:23,900 --> 00:06:25,100
Could be a moltoxin?

00:06:25,100 --> 00:06:26,700
Could be a pesticide?

00:06:26,700 --> 00:06:27,660
Could be an herbicide?

00:06:27,660 --> 00:06:28,780
Could be a heavy metal?

00:06:28,780 --> 00:06:31,380
Could be a bacteria?

00:06:31,380 --> 00:06:33,220
Could be a lime bacteria?

00:06:33,220 --> 00:06:34,540
Could be a fungus?

00:06:34,540 --> 00:06:36,540
Could be a virus?

00:06:36,540 --> 00:06:38,780
Something gets inside the cell

00:06:38,780 --> 00:06:41,980
and causes the cell to go into rapid replication

00:06:41,980 --> 00:06:44,020
and then it replicates cells

00:06:44,020 --> 00:06:47,420
that are also equally dysfunctioning

00:06:47,420 --> 00:06:49,220
in a state of rapid replication.

00:06:49,220 --> 00:06:51,340
That's what cancer is.

00:06:51,340 --> 00:06:52,340
Where that happens,

00:06:52,340 --> 00:06:56,180
you have lots of different tumor suppressor genes.

00:06:56,180 --> 00:07:00,620
Right now, there's no about 25 different families

00:07:00,620 --> 00:07:03,380
of tumor suppressor genes that will turn on

00:07:03,380 --> 00:07:07,540
and help cause that cell to go to die.

00:07:07,540 --> 00:07:12,380
It's an internal stimulation of in,

00:07:12,380 --> 00:07:15,260
what's called an intrinsic apoptotic pathway.

00:07:15,260 --> 00:07:17,700
It causes that cell to die.

00:07:17,700 --> 00:07:19,940
If you have defects in those genes,

00:07:19,940 --> 00:07:24,780
you can have a more difficult time killing cancer

00:07:24,780 --> 00:07:29,580
because that you're completely reliant on the external pathway

00:07:29,660 --> 00:07:32,300
or the extrinsic apoptotic pathway.

00:07:32,300 --> 00:07:35,260
Something killing the cell from the outside,

00:07:35,260 --> 00:07:37,460
your immune system killing the cell from the outside.

00:07:37,460 --> 00:07:39,380
That's what we're trying to do with the right machine,

00:07:39,380 --> 00:07:42,100
stimulate in a viewed response on the cell

00:07:42,100 --> 00:07:43,740
to kill the cell from the outside,

00:07:43,740 --> 00:07:47,900
stimulate an extrinsic apoptotic pathway.

00:07:48,780 --> 00:07:51,420
That's what we're trying to do with nutrition.

00:07:51,420 --> 00:07:53,180
That's what you're trying to do with dietary,

00:07:53,180 --> 00:07:54,540
that's what you're trying to do with everything else

00:07:54,540 --> 00:07:56,980
to try to do with the chemotherapy,

00:07:56,980 --> 00:07:59,460
stimulate that extrinsic pathway.

00:07:59,460 --> 00:08:02,380
Well, your body has this intrinsic pathway

00:08:02,380 --> 00:08:04,900
through the tumor suppressor genes.

00:08:04,900 --> 00:08:06,300
What do we have defects on those genes?

00:08:06,300 --> 00:08:09,560
We have a more difficult time killing cancer

